      ":question/id": "86112d28-25a2-5d86-9c7b-fc0c2d1692c9",
      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-65438",
      ":question/problem": "$\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-{45}^{∘})=$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Recall the difference formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u-v)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v-\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\n$$\n\nApplying the difference formula for sine with $u=x$ and $v={45}^{∘},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-{45}^{∘}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡{45}^{∘}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡{45}^{∘} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot \\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot \\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{2}-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x).\\end{aligned}\n$$"
    },
