      ":question/id": "2aa915f6-8e31-5601-8256-7110f8cdfa0f",
      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-329179",
      ":question/problem": "Express $\\operatorname{sin}(x+{240}^{∘})$ in terms of $\\operatorname{sin}x$ and $\\operatorname{cos}x.$\n\n$\\operatorname{sin}(x+{240}^{∘})=$\n{{field-1}}$\\operatorname{sin}x\\,-$\n{{field-2}}$\\operatorname{cos}x$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Recall the sum formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}(u+v)=\\operatorname{sin}u\\operatorname{cos}v+\\operatorname{cos}u\\operatorname{sin}v\n$$\n\nApplying the sum formula for sine with $u=x$ and $v={240}^{∘},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}(x+{240}^{∘}) & =\\operatorname{sin}x\\operatorname{cos}{240}^{∘}+\\operatorname{cos}x\\operatorname{sin}{240}^{∘} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}x\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right)+\\operatorname{cos}x\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\operatorname{sin}x-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\,\\operatorname{cos}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
    },
