      ":question/id": "6c821975-da43-58e6-b429-87f2ab061604",
      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-332176",
      ":question/problem": "Express $\\operatorname{sin}(x-{225}^{∘})$ in terms of $\\operatorname{sin}x$ and $\\operatorname{cos}x.$\n\n$\\operatorname{sin}(x-{225}^{∘})=$\n{{field-1}}$\\operatorname{sin}x\\,+$\n{{field-2}}$\\operatorname{cos}x$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Recall the difference formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}(u-v)=\\operatorname{sin}u\\operatorname{cos}v-\\operatorname{cos}u\\operatorname{sin}v\n$$\n\nApplying the difference formula for sine with $u=x$ and $v={225}^{∘},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}(x-{225}^{∘}) & =\\operatorname{sin}x\\operatorname{cos}{225}^{∘}-\\operatorname{cos}x\\operatorname{sin}{225}^{∘} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}x\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right)-\\operatorname{cos}x\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\,\\operatorname{sin}x+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\,\\operatorname{cos}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\,\\operatorname{sin}x+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\,\\operatorname{cos}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
    },
