      ":question/id": "9a81f8fe-16ea-565d-8f32-af073a7db052",
      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-141270",
      ":question/problem": "$\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+{135}^{∘})=$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Recall the sum formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u+v)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v+\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\n$$\n\nApplying the sum formula for sine with $u=x$ and $v={135}^{∘},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+{135}^{∘}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡{135}^{∘}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡{135}^{∘} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot \\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{2}+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
    },
