      ":question/id": "9b662a6f-66f3-5ffb-bf0b-66a90ae7e592",
      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-141271",
      ":question/problem": "$\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+{150}^{∘})=$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Recall the sum formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u+v)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v+\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\n$$\n\nApplying the sum formula for sine with $u=x$ and $v={150}^{∘},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+{150}^{∘}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡{150}^{∘}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡{150}^{∘} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot \\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{2}+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
    },
