      ":question/id": "b6e1f817-7c7e-51c8-bd09-e888759f9be3",
      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-141275",
      ":question/problem": "$\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-{120}^{∘})=$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Recall the difference formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u-v)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v-\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\n$$\n\nApplying the difference formula for sine with $u=x$ and $v={120}^{∘},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-{120}^{∘}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡{120}^{∘}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡{120}^{∘} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot \\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{2}-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
    },
