      ":question/id": "bfc5afd1-9723-5b19-a1e3-57f1ad1233ac",
      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-332178",
      ":question/problem": "Express $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-{300}^{∘})$ in terms of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$\n\n$\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-{300}^{∘})=$\n{{field-1}}$\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,+$\n{{field-2}}$\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Recall the difference formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u-v)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v-\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\n$$\n\nApplying the difference formula for sine with $u=x$ and $v={300}^{∘},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-{300}^{∘}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡{300}^{∘}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡{300}^{∘} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot \\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
    },
