      ":question/id": "da4f3b0b-e716-525b-97e5-9d6526f804b7",
      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-332180",
      ":question/problem": "Express $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-{330}^{∘})$ in terms of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$\n\n$\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-{330}^{∘})=$\n{{field-1}}$\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,+$\n{{field-2}}$\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Recall the difference formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u-v)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v-\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\n$$\n\nApplying the difference formula for sine with $u=x$ and $v={330}^{∘},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-{330}^{∘}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡{330}^{∘}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡{330}^{∘} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot \\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
    },
