      ":question/id": "01bece61-4e20-59b8-ba47-2811024557f8",
      ":question/problem": "Express $\\sin(x+300^\\circ)$ using $\\sin x$ and $\\cos x$. Enter exact coefficients.\n\n$\\sin(x+300^\\circ)=$ {{field-1}} $\\sin x\\,-$ {{field-2}} $\\cos x$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Recall the sum formula for sine:\n$$\n\\sin(u+v)=\\sin u\\cos v+\\cos u\\sin v.\n$$\nThe angle $300^\\circ$ lies in quadrant IV with reference angle $60^\\circ$, so\n$$\n\\cos300^\\circ=\\frac12,\\qquad \\sin300^\\circ=-\\frac{\\sqrt3}{2}.\n$$\nSubstituting into the sum formula gives\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\sin(x+300^\\circ)&=\\sin x\\cos300^\\circ+\\cos x\\sin300^\\circ\\\\\n&=\\sin x\\cdot\\frac12+\\cos x\\cdot\\left(-\\frac{\\sqrt3}{2}\\right)\\\\\n&=\\frac12\\sin x-\\frac{\\sqrt3}{2}\\cos x.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nThe minus sign is already supplied before the second blank, so the entries are $\\frac12$ and $\\frac{\\sqrt3}{2}$."
    },
    {
      ":db/id": 17592186701660,
