      ":question/id": "510d0ad5-a38a-5942-b886-27217a13f30c",
      ":question/problem": "Express $\\sin(x+90^\\circ)$ in terms of $\\sin x$ or $\\cos x$.\n\n$\\sin(x+90^\\circ)=$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Recall the sum formula for sine:\n$$\n\\sin(u+v)=\\sin u\\cos v+\\cos u\\sin v.\n$$\nApply it with $u=x$ and $v=90^\\circ$. Since $\\cos90^\\circ=0$ and $\\sin90^\\circ=1$,\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\sin(x+90^\\circ)&=\\sin x\\cos90^\\circ+\\cos x\\sin90^\\circ\\\\\n&=\\sin x\\cdot0+\\cos x\\cdot1\\\\\n&=\\cos x.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"
    },
