      ":question/problem": "Express $\\sin(x-150^\\circ)$ using $\\sin x$ and $\\cos x$.\n\n$\\sin(x-150^\\circ)=$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Use the difference formula for sine:\n$$\n\\sin(u-v)=\\sin u\\cos v-\\cos u\\sin v.\n$$\nApply it and substitute the exact special-angle values:\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\sin(x-150^\\circ)&=\\sin x\\cos 150^\\circ-\\cos x\\sin 150^\\circ\\\\\n&=\\sin x\\cdot\\left(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right)-\\cos x\\cdot\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)\\\\\n&=-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\sin x-\\frac{1}{2}\\cos x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"
