      },
      ":question/id": "2f5a97b8-e8e8-53aa-b432-81ebac89487f",
      ":question/problem": "Express $\\sin(x+60^\\circ)+\\sin(x+315^\\circ)$ in the form $A\\sin x+B\\cos x$. Enter exact, signed coefficients.\n\n$A=$ {{field-1}}\n\n$B=$ {{field-2}}",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Use the sum formula for sine:\n$$\n\\sin(u+v)=\\sin u\\cos v+\\cos u\\sin v.\n$$\nUse the sum formula for sine:\n$$\n\\sin(u+v)=\\sin u\\cos v+\\cos u\\sin v.\n$$\nExpand the two terms separately:\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\sin(x+60^\\circ)&=\\sin x\\cos 60^\\circ+\\cos x\\sin 60^\\circ\\\\\n&=\\sin x\\cdot\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)+\\cos x\\cdot\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right)\\\\\n&=\\frac{1}{2}\\sin x+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\cos x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\sin(x+315^\\circ)&=\\sin x\\cos 315^\\circ+\\cos x\\sin 315^\\circ\\\\\n&=\\sin x\\cdot\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right)+\\cos x\\cdot\\left(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right)\\\\\n&=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\sin x-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\cos x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nLet $E$ denote the original expression. Add the entire second expansion and collect like terms:\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nE&=\\left(\\frac{1}{2}+\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right)\\right)\\sin x\\\\\n&\\quad+\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}+\\left(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right)\\right)\\cos x\\\\\n&=\\left(\\frac{1+\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right)\\sin x\\\\\n&\\quad+\\left(\\frac{-\\sqrt{2}+\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right)\\cos x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nThus $A=\\frac{1+\\sqrt{2}}{2}$ and $B=\\frac{-\\sqrt{2}+\\sqrt{3}}{2}$."
    },
    {
