      ":question/id": "711dc95a-a8ca-5205-ae27-22364c41033b",
      ":question/problem": "Express $\\sin(x-330^\\circ)+\\sin(x+330^\\circ)$ in the form $A\\sin x+B\\cos x$. Enter exact, signed coefficients.\n\n$A=$ {{field-1}}\n\n$B=$ {{field-2}}",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Use the difference formula for sine:\n$$\n\\sin(u-v)=\\sin u\\cos v-\\cos u\\sin v.\n$$\nUse the sum formula for sine:\n$$\n\\sin(u+v)=\\sin u\\cos v+\\cos u\\sin v.\n$$\nExpand the two terms separately:\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\sin(x-330^\\circ)&=\\sin x\\cos 330^\\circ-\\cos x\\sin 330^\\circ\\\\\n&=\\sin x\\cdot\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right)-\\cos x\\cdot\\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right)\\\\\n&=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\sin x+\\frac{1}{2}\\cos x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\sin(x+330^\\circ)&=\\sin x\\cos 330^\\circ+\\cos x\\sin 330^\\circ\\\\\n&=\\sin x\\cdot\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right)+\\cos x\\cdot\\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right)\\\\\n&=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\sin x-\\frac{1}{2}\\cos x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nLet $E$ denote the original expression. Add the entire second expansion and collect like terms:\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nE&=\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}+\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right)\\right)\\sin x\\\\\n&\\quad+\\left(\\frac{1}{2}+\\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right)\\right)\\cos x\\\\\n&=\\left(\\sqrt{3}\\right)\\sin x\\\\\n&\\quad+\\left(0\\right)\\cos x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nThus $A=\\sqrt{3}$ and $B=0$."
    },
